Basis and assumptions.

The harness is built from nothing, with no existing code assumed. Phase 1 is the largest build of the reports: the settings-file layout for a check, the Jira fetch with caching and a check that the data is complete, the rules (a field is filled in, a value is in an allowed list, a field is filled in only when another condition holds), the results written as metric records, the run-recording comment, the entry point that takes a ticket, and the Confluence Cloud helper, with tests that make no real API calls.
The monthly report is the largest later report build, because it generates a new report for two instances, has to match the dashboard, and publishes with a hold; the structure report needs a rule over the Initiative, Milestone and Epic hierarchy; the risk report needs two age rules; the notifier shares a mail helper with AUTO-103; the summary is mostly trend computation, a number check, the approval transition and the guidance file with its preview, with a small model call. Phase 4 polls for new tickets, maps each to its report and period, and avoids running a ticket twice.
Phases 7 and 8 are the common display. Phase 8's size depends on the platform Phase 0 chooses. The other Ideas that emit records (AUTO-106, AUTO-103, AUTO-84 to AUTO-87, AUTO-290, AUTO-27) have not been re-estimated for emitting records; each Idea's Phase 0 re-checks.
The hours assume polling works and hosting is available. They do not include the Odd Squad team's time, the experts' time, access to the SharePoint instructions, permission to send as the Odd Squad email address, cleaning up TDIR, or a Jira administrator's work to add the approval statuses and transitions.
These are judgment estimates, not measurements. Phase 0 re-checks them once the harness is designed.
